WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.470
Hazuki, your text came so late!

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.140
You should've called me!

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.430
If you'd told me you were at the shop...

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.300
<i>What in the world?</i>

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.430
<i>I have no idea</i>

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.310
<i>which one of them it is...</i>

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.270
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.020
This is obstruction of someone's business...

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.310
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.570
President Octopus.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.940
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:17.250
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:23.420
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:29.970
I was prepared for the time you left

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:36.810
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:43.320
After I embraced you with all I had

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:52.870
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:56.540
filled my heart

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:03.040
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:09.720
You gave me happiness

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.050
Until I meet you again one day

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.560
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.100
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.770
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.900
I won't forget your smile

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.040
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.250
<i>Katakana...
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b></i>

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.580
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:57.890
Hey.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.140
Why do you write sentences in katakana instead of standard hiragana?

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.270
How long have you been standing there?

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.350
Huh?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.560
Did I see something I shouldn't've?

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.730
You should've said something.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.730
If you really didn't want me to see it, you should've been sneakier about it.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.150
True...

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.070
So?

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:12.980
What?

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.030
Why do you write everything other than kanji in katakana?

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.280
For the mood.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.910
It expresses my mood, kind of.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.700
Really?

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.040
Actually, I want it to look like a doctor's chart...

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.290
The kind that's written in German?

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.460
I want the horizontal writing to be decorative.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.590
Like this...

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.840
Why do you like that style?

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.140
Come on, it's obvious.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.470
Don't ask me silly questions.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.220
But I don't know!

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:43.970
It's elegant.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.440
See? I knew you'd laugh.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.480
No, I'm not...

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.230
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.240
Not here.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.740
His sketchbook...

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.340
<i>Flower shears, clippers...</i>

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:14.840
<i>The florist knife, too...</i>

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.590
His<i> tools...</i>

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.470
<i>They're all gone.</i>

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.480
<i>I mean, it's strange.</i>

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:36.400
<i>He only used the flowers that I love to make all of these arrangements.</i>

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:37.900
<i>That's right.</i>

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.610
<i>This arrangement was his first birthday present to me.</i>

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.910
<i>That one was for Christmas.</i>

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.040
<i>That was for my first birthday after we got married.</i>

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.660
<i>Next to it, my second birthday.</i>

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.370
<i>For Halloween...</i>

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.630
<i>That one was for Christmas, too.</i>

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.090
<i>Our last Girls' Day together...</i>

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.380
<i>New Year's...</i>

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.220
<i>The bouquets Shimao gave me...</i>

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.760
<i>I could never forget them.</i>

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.390
<i>What in god's name is going on?</i>

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:30.700
We are all alive.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:35.750
We're alive, so we're singing this song.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:40.670
We are all alive.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.470
We're alive, so...

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.140
Damn.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.110
<i>I withdrew the maximum amount.</i>

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.150
<i>Even though Rokka didn't touch this money I had tucked away...</i>

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:06.070
<i>If the police are called, I get nabbed,</i>

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.370
<i>and then explain the whole situation,</i>

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.660
<i>Hazuki will be treated like a lunatic.</i>

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:15.580
What?

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.580
<i>The police, already?</i>

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.590
<b>Manager</b>

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.350
<i>Just a little...</i>

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.940
<i>I'll just listen to her voice.</i>

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.530
When you came to the shop,

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.000
did you go upstairs?

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.620
I can't find the gray backpack.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.880
That, and...

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.960
a potted plant.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.880
The one that was next to the window in my husband's room.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.510
Snow-in-Summer...

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.930
If you've got it with you,

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.020
I'd like you to return it.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:19.810
Please.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.900
Stealing is wrong.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.700
If there's an explanation,

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.320
tell me.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.870
<i>You've got it wrong, Rokka.</i>

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.620
<i>It's Hazuki who stole things away.</i>

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.430
In exchange for losing her voice, the mermaid princess got legs,

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:52.140
but when she walked, she felt excruciating pain.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.770
I'm fine, though.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.890
The reason is I wasn't a mermaid to begin with.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.600
Lucky you. Looks like you're having fun.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.900
"Live a pleasant life in the unpleasant world."

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.730
Huh?

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.990
Takasugi Shinsaku.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.490
That's my motto.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.240
The prince keeps me waiting and waiting, so I've got all this free time.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:15.620
I wonder if that stupid prince even intends to come.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:19.120
In my experience, I haven't seen anyone who's stupider than you.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.130
If you say it while looking like that, you'll hurt my feelings.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.150
Where are you?

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:43.770
Where are you going?

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:46.980
Everyone, look at this!

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.150
It's like a huge mirror!

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:51.030
Beautiful...

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.200
It's like from a dream.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.700
You said the same thing about the place they introduced last week.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.040
Bora Bora Island!

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:59.660
That was amazing too, wasn't it?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.460
Would you like to go?

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:02.290
Yeah.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:03.130
Me too.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:08.420
But I don't know if I'll ever get to go to a faraway place like that.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.430
At the moment, it's kind of out of the question,

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:14.640
but as long as it's only for a short time, I'm sure you'll be able to go.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:15.930
Yeah...

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.680
<i>Not even close to "kind of"...</i>

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.560
<i>Those words don't give me any comfort,</i>

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.520
<i>when just walking 100 meters leaves me breathless.</i>

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.030
The answer is "cleaning."

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.650
Greetings from Odaiba.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:36.910
The sky is deep blue again today as we
broadcast to you live from Hachitama.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:40.830
I'm serious about my dream, ya know?!
Why're you standin' in my way?!

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:41.750
We're outta here, Kaori!

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:47.290
This is Yousuke, the souvenir shop's pet
that eats the local pickled vegetables...

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.170
I'm gonna turn it off.
This is Yousuke, the souvenir shop's pet
that eats the local pickled vegetables...

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.970
Rokka, you've got a quirky side.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:55.430
How so?

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:57.470
We didn't go on a honeymoon.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.350
In fact, the farthest we've gone together is a 1000-yen, round-trip train to a mountain for hiking,

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.810
yet every time you watch a travel show, you say, "Let's go there someday."

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.940
Well, after all, I do want to go someday.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:11.440
If you remarry someone who'll take you there someday, be my guest.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.320
Don't say that.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:15.780
At this rate, you won't be able to go.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.160
Well, to be honest, anywhere would be fine.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.540
In other words, here is fine, too.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:31.960
As long as we can be together, anything is fine.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.810
I'm surprised you can say that without getting embarrassed.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.520
You can be really prickly sometimes, Shimao.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.940
Better than fawning over someone all the time, like you.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:56.490
<i>The potted plant is gone.</i>

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.280
<i>Is it because I was dragging my heels?</i>

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:05.910
When I die, will you eat a little bit of my bones?

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.580
<i>I was right.</i>

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.460
<i>These letters...</i>

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.970
Oh, my! What, is there a store grand opening or something tomorrow?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.430
Nothing beats lots of orders.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:20.260
I like this one that uses vegetables.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:21.760
Asparagus?

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:27.350
It's rare for you to ask me for a favor, Rokka, so I don't mind at all.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:29.150
And you know I like to get involved.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:33.360
But in exchange, when things are settled, explain it to me, okay?

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.610
And if any trouble comes up, contact me right away.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:37.820
I will.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:39.780
I promise.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:42.410
Don't worry. Go on.

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:46.290
I won't forget this.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:51.540
Thank you for being accepting of my sudden peculiar behavior.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.930
<i>It's my first time walking without a destination in mind.</i>

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.310
<i>Even though there's certainly someone I'm in love with,</i>

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.430
<i>for me not to know who it is...</i>

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:11.060
<i>I've never heard of such an irresponsible crush.</i>

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.360
<i>It's a thief's destiny to be caught.</i>

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.820
<i>Who's my adversary, the Fiend with Twenty Faces?</i>

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.170
I shrunk.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:36.960
<i>The miniature version...</i>

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.340
<i>She's too adorable this way.</i>

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.930
You didn't do it yourself.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:45.220
I don't have the power to do that.

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:46.930
Only the prince can do it.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:50.480
<i>I wish she would stop looking up at me like that.</i>

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.560
<i>It's like she makes me want to run away.</i>

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:57.690
Maybe he's gone back to drawing picture books again.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.570
Picture books?

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:02.610
He's using my body to draw pictures?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.830
I always got low grades in art, so is he gonna be okay?

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:16.590
<i>It cools off a little when the sun goes down.</i>

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:21.590
<i>That reminds me, even though Rokka gets cold easily, she wore that outfit...</i>

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:25.350
I missed my chance to warn her.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:34.560
It's cold!

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.500
<i>Really, I want to walk next to her,</i>

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.500
<i>but the distance between us isn't getting any shorter.</i>

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:10.430
Hey, excuse me...

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.140
Don't space out. Listen to me.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.060
I was listening.

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:17.560
Are you sure?

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.150
Yeah.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.990
Then can you make it just like I explained?

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:24.650
Wrapping it in a cylinder shape, was it?

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.910
You can wrap it in a round shape, right?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.070
Yeah...

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.280
Hey!

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:32.500
You lost consciousness for just a moment, didn't you?

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:36.370
Jeez, that's dangerous...

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:37.960
Now that you mention it,

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.670
it seemed like I was in the shop, learning how to put together bouquets.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.130
But why?

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:46.130
With your physical body gone, if you just keep pondering things,

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:48.140
your ego will get bloated.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:51.220
I mean, if memories appear in your consciousness,

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.890
you really may not be able to return.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.560
What? I don't get it.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.940
Don't suddenly spring tough concepts on me.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.230
And you're saying scary things with no hesitation...

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.530
Knock it off!

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:08.780
Anyway, you absolutely have to remember that you're trapped inside of a drawing.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:14.540
Otherwise, you might mistakenly step into a grave and not even notice it.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.420
What?! As if I'd let something stupid like that happen!

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:19.630
You are stupid, for suddenly being afraid just now.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:22.000
After all, that's, you know...

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.800
At the end of the day, it's like it's happening to a stand-in.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.050
What is that?!

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.720
A guy can only take so much tragedy.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.180
The curtain's closing already on this anonymous 22-year-old life?

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.850
Give me a break!

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:36.600
Then you'd better find a way home quickly, huh?

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:38.020
That's what I'm talking about!

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.100
Hazuki.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.990
Do you have a minute before you go home?

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:48.490
Isn't this the kind of plant you like, Hazuki?

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.990
That's an interesting color.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.990
Like gold, but also close to red...

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:55.080
It's hard to describe.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.330
<i>But what's the bandage for?</i>

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:00.830
The color is close to your shirt today.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.260
Now that you mention it, I think I see it.

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.510
So here.

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:09.340
To commemorate working here for half a year.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.340
I can keep it?

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.560
Just my little way of saying thanks.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:18.060
Copper Spoons.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:21.020
This is Copper Spoons?

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:24.320
Succulents have a lot of fun names, don't they?

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:27.490
Actually, these are two flowers planted together

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:30.700
and the small one is called "Silver Spoons."

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:31.780
Similar, right?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:35.290
They're all cute, though, aren't they?

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:37.580
Yeah.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:41.540
<i>Actually, I'm feeling deja vu here.</i>

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.540
<i>Trying to look tough?</i>

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.050
<i>When I was still a regular customer,</i>

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:52.550
<i>my attention was idly drawn one day...</i>

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:56.430
<i>I never imagined I'd be asking her directly in the future.</i>

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.560
<i>I'm proud of myself from then.</i>

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:05.070
It's not even worth talking about...

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:08.820
but I'll let you in on it.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:12.070
<i>It seems she gets scratched by a hook hanging on her closet once in a while.</i>

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.320
Ow!

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:16.330
<i>Certainly, it's no big thing.</i>

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:17.740
<i>And yet,</i>

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.580
<i>it feels like my heart is going to burst.</i>

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.210
<i>Cute...</i>

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.340
I'm telling you...

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.760
You're getting too wrapped up in the past!

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.930
Do you intend to live only in your memories?

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.840
I... Again?

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:38.310
You just get swept up so easily.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.310
I'm being swept up? By who?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.310
Is that old man doing something on the other side?

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.320
You don't understand.

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:53.570
Contrary to "till death do us part,"

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:57.660
if you underestimate the adamant stubbornness of someone who can't pass on,

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.950
even after death,

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.830
you'll never make it back home alive.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:05.580
The weird thing is...

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:10.170
you told me we're in one of the prince's picture books,

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:14.590
but going by your words, I don't get the sense that the prince created it on purpose.

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:16.640
I wonder why.

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:25.850
Because part of him really does want the princess to be free.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.860
<i>I realize that not everything is cut and dry...</i>

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.200
<i>but I'll seriously never forgive him.</i>

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.380
Making you cry like that

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:53.630
tells me he made a lot of mistakes.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:19:00.810
<i>I would do anything for the manager's sake.</i>

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:09.900
<i>But if that meant making it so she resumes her life with her former husband,</i>

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:12.650
<i>where does that leave me?</i>

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:13.900
<i>That's the question.</i>

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:41.180
No, no, no. That's a mistake. Yeah...

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:44.430
Scary.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.730
I think I was on the verge of thinking the unthinkable.

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.610
I mean, I made a promise.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.070
That I would live longer than her.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:55.940
You're silly.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.990
Yeah, that's why I ended up here, right?

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:00.320
Yep.

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.080
You don't have to agree right away.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:03.830
After all...

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:07.080
After all, what?

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:13.550
Hey.

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.840
I guess I still can't

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:23.850
get over Shimao.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.230
So what?!

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.730
That has nothing to do with whether I throw in the towel or not!

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.210
<i>Even if the manager isn't waiting for me in the future,</i>

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:57.300
<i>I'll do anything to meet her.</i>

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:01.630
<i>I'll do what I can, and if it doesn't work, it doesn't work.</i>

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:05.640
<i>Even with that in mind, I have to give it my all...</i>

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:10.640
<i>since I'd hate to follow in that ghost's footsteps!</i>

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:25.370
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:31.120
you always smile

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:35.210
Tell me why

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:39.090
it won't go away

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:40.880
I gave you everything

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.720
You gave me anything

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:47.510
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:49.180
still my everything

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.390
I love you

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:55.770
It is a miracle

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:58.900
like fleeting snow

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:04.860
that fell in summer

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:11.870
If I hadn't met you

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:15.080
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:22.590
and nothing would have pressed down on my chest

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:28.260
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:35.310
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:40.440
When I close my eyes

00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:44.450
you're right beside me
